#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
cell — isolated environments for AI agent CLIs.

Like Python venvs, but for AI runtimes: each agent gets its own config,
API key, model, persona and memory — scoped to the project you run it in.

Design goals (and why):
  * One file, Python standard library only. You can read every line of
    what you are running. No build step, no dependencies, no supply chain.
  * Runtimes and providers are DATA (tables in your config file), not
    code. Adding a new AI CLI or a new LLM subscription never requires
    editing this script: `cell runtime add`, `cell provider add`.
  * Nothing is hidden: `cell show` prints the exact environment, files
    and command before anything launches, with secrets masked.
  * Secrets never land inside your project: API keys live in
    ~/.config/cell/config.toml (chmod 600) or in env vars, and reach the
    runtime only through the process environment at launch.

Config:  ~/.config/cell/config.toml   (override with $CELL_HOME)
Usage:   cell            (interactive menu)
         cell --help     (all commands)
"""

